A class diagram showing attributes of Person and Simulation classes, methods of both
classes, their parameters, parameter types and return types. Attributes, methods with
parameter listing, parameter types and return types for any other classes you add.

Person:
    Attributes:
        name: str
        is_literate: bool
        savings: float
        checking: float
        debt: float
        debt_payed: float
        mortgage: float
        mortgage_payed: float
        loan: float
        year: float
        has_house: bool
        has_dog: bool
        has_had_dog: bool
        years_with_dog: int
    Methods:
        __init__(name: str, is_literate: bool) -> None
        get_wealth() -> lst of float
        annual_to_accounts() -> None
        annual_interest() -> None
        monthly_debt() -> None
        monthly_rent() -> None
        buy_house() -> None
        mortgage_payment() -> None
        buy_dog() -> None
        pay_for_dog() -> None
        run_a_year() -> None

Simulation:
    Attributes:
        person: person
        years: int
        lst: list
        years_in_debt: int
        years_renting: int
    Methods:
        __init__(person: Person, years: int) -> None
        run(): list of float
        summary() -> dictionary


