Answers to the following questions
What did you learn from this assignment that you didn’t know before?

 - Honestly, I didn't really realize how the ways you decide to allocate your money can make such a difference over time. I feel
 like now I have to be more prepared for the future, at least for once I get an actual job with adult financial decisions to make.

How much more debt did NFL end up paying compared to FL?
 - $2938

How many more years was NFL in debt compared to FL?
 - 14 years

How much more money does FL have at the end of 40 years compared to NFL?
 - $1,992,129

Which decision in your model had the greatest effect on the disparity between NFL
and FL?
 - I think it's either when they decide to buy a house or it's putting the savings in a bank vs a mutual fund

A brief description of the work done for “your touch” part.
 - I added the expense of getting a dog. Once a house with a yard is bought, a dog is bought. Every year, there are basic expenses
 that need to be paid every year. Every three years, the dog has some sort of medical emergency or surgery that needs to be paid for.
 Finally, the dog dies after 12 years

